{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98616","published":"2026-11-13T12:06:37.188502Z","modified":"2026-11-13T12:45:13.979626451Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-100236","CVE-2026-86561","CVE-2026-86562","CVE-2026-86563","CVE-2026-86565","CVE-2026-86566","CVE-2026-86567","CVE-2026-86845","CVE-2026-86846","CVE-2026-86847","CVE-2026-86848","CVE-2026-86849","CVE-2026-86856","CVE-2026-93683"],"summary":"Important: dpdk security update","details":"The dpdk packages provide the Data Plane Development Kit, which is a set of libraries and drivers for fast packet processing in the user space.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Missing memory size validation before mmap in vhost memory region setup (CVE-2026-86561)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Control-queue descriptor double-fetch overflows host heap in DPDK vhost (VDUSE) (CVE-2026-86562)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Double offset bug in vhost log mapping calculation (CVE-2026-86563)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest can desynchronize virtqueue size from inflight descriptor table size, causing out-of-bounds write (CVE-2026-86565)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest with runt RX descriptors underflows copy length in vhost enqueue (split and packed rings) (CVE-2026-86566)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: VDUSE handler fails to invalidate vring pointers when IOTLB is invalidated, leading to use-after-unmap (CVE-2026-86567)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest-triggered use-after-free and type confusion in vhost-crypto session cleanup (CVE-2026-86845)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest can trigger out-of-bounds write by controlling avail ring index in vhost-crypto (CVE-2026-86846)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest can trigger infinite loop in vhost-crypto writeback chain cleanup (CVE-2026-86847)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Time-of-check/time-of-use vulnerability allowing guest-triggered out-of-bounds write in vhost-crypto (CVE-2026-86848)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Integer overflow combined with missing validation leads to host buffer overflow in vhost-crypto (CVE-2026-86849)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Stack and heap buffer overflow in nfp vDPA driver (CVE-2026-86856)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: Guest-triggered out-of-bounds walk via vhost indirect descriptor length TOCTOU (CVE-2026-93683)\n\n* dpdk: dpdk: heap out-of-bounds read/write in GSO header copy (CVE-2026-100236)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dpdk-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/dpdk-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:25.11-2.el10_2"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98616.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dpdk-tools","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/dpdk-tools?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:25.11-2.el10_2"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98616.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dpdk-devel","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/dpdk-devel?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:25.11-2.el10_2"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98616.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dpdk-debugsource","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/dpdk-debugsource?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:25.11-2.el10_2"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98616.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dpdk","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/roc